2.3 Users are permitted to use the functional features of the Software and generate or export software operation data and reports for their own legitimate business use. Users are not entitled to secondary distribution, resale or sub-licensing rights of any kind.
3. Prohibited Behaviors (Core Closed-Source and Paid Restrictions)
3.1 Prohibition of Open Source and Information Leakage: Any act of extracting, reverse engineering, decompiling, disassembling or cracking the Software’s source code and core logic is strictly forbidden. Disseminating or disclosing the Software source code, crack patches, core configurations and internal documents on any network platform, open-source community or third-party channel is prohibited.
3.2 Prohibition of Unauthorized Distribution: It is strictly prohibited to share, copy, disseminate or sell the Software installation package, program body, cracked version or modified version through free or paid channels, including but not limited to network disk sharing, community dissemination and bulk distribution.
3.3 Prohibition of Tampering and Secondary Development: Without formal written authorization from the copyright owner, users are not allowed to modify, delete or add software functions, encapsulate secondary versions, develop derivative tools or adapt third-party plugins for the Software.
3.4 Prohibition of Unauthorized Commercial Use: Unauthorized use, cracked use, commercial use beyond authorization scope, multi-person sharing of a single license and unauthorized license transfer are all regarded as infringing commercial behaviors, for which the copyright owner reserves the right to pursue legal liabilities.
4. Paid Authorization Rules
4.1 The only valid basis for legal use of the Software is official paid purchase plus exclusive authorization credentials. Any use without valid authorization credentials constitutes illegal infringement.
4.2 Different paid packages correspond to different usage permissions, device quotas, service cycles and after-sales rights. Users shall strictly abide by package specifications, and any out-of-scope use shall be deemed a breach of agreement.
